# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Showreel
#
# Versioned (the reproducible source of truth): render.cjs, fetch-sources.cjs,
# timeline.json, sources.json, the two markdown docs, the render inputs under
# showreel/assets/branding and showreel/assets/fonts, plus the lightweight
# delivery artefacts (poster.jpg, contact-sheet.jpg, render-report.json).
#
# Ignored: everything that `npm run showreel:render` can rebuild, every
# multi-hundred-megabyte local source mirror, and the finished master itself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Rebuildable render intermediates (~3.3 GB).
showreel/build/

# High-resolution source mirrors kept locally only. Their public URLs and the
# exact yt-dlp formats are versioned in showreel/sources.json, so
# `npm run showreel:sources` restores them.
showreel/assets/source/*.webm
showreel/assets/source/*.mp4
showreel/assets/source/*.mkv
showreel/source-films/

# Draft deliveries stay local. The selected website master is versioned so a
# clean GitHub Pages checkout can build the same page that was reviewed locally.
showreel/output/*.mp4
!showreel/output/igor-szuniewicz-showreel-2026.mp4

# REAPER peak cache and scratch/staging folders from editing sessions.
showreel/output/peaks/
showreel/_an/
showreel/_to_delete/

# Personal / working files — never publish
*.b64
akademiki-graz*
utwory-katalog.xlsx

# Python cache from the CV generator.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
